{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtPYfdfg8eSPg6YZgZUd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The cache split is in `bot.py`, but on this prompt it probably won't take effect until the static part grows, so I left that decision to you.\n\n**What was wrong:** `build_system()` put the instructions and the athlete's facts in one text block with a single cache marker. Every `save_fact` changed the facts, which changed the prefix hash, so the whole prompt was re-cached. That matches `logs/usage.jsonl`: the call after each save shows `cache_read` at 0 and `cache_creation` back at the full prompt size.\n\n**What I changed:** `build_system()` now returns two cached blocks. Block one is the constant instructions. Block two is the per-athlete tail: date, profile, zones, goal, facts and language. A memory write now only invalidates block two. Nothing else in the request changed.\n\n**Verification:** I added `test_cache_split.py` with 5 tests, and they pass. They check the two markers, that the instructions block is byte-identical across athletes, days and fact lists, and that a fact changes only the tail. Against the original code, 4 fail and 1 errors. I did not make any API calls: there is no `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY` here and the SDK isn't installed.\n\n**The open issue:** Anthropic won't cache a prefix shorter than the model's minimum, which is 1024 tokens for `claude-sonnet-4-5`. The instructions are about 2,500 characters and the core tool schemas about 420 characters, roughly 950–1000 tokens together. The first log line with no facts already shows a 1024-token cache write. So the marker after the instructions is likely ignored, and the fix does nothing until the static part is over 1024 tokens. I didn't pad the prompt, because that changes its content and cost. I recommend adding about 200–300 tokens of real static content, such as worked session examples. `ANSWER.md` explains this and says what to check in `usage.jsonl` after deploy.\n\n**From the colleague's note:** I applied the two-marker split, the byte-stable static block, keeping tools fixed within a loop, and checking `usage` after deploy. I did not apply the claim that a ~780-token static block gets its own cache entry, since that fails at this size. Top-N fact selection and the 4-marker limit don't apply here.\n\n**Not changed:** keyword-based tool groups still cause a full cache miss when a message adds a group, since tools sit before the system prompt. The log shows this with `plan_week` and `predict_race`. This was an existing trade-off and I left it alone.\n\nNothing is committed. Files changed: `bot.py`, plus new `test_cache_split.py` and `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2105,"cache_read_input_tokens":45950,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2105},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41794d17-ecb5-4ef3-8146-010b64f1b684","uuid":"f70ce231-9eb3-4082-8bd7-f15b41acb728","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:35:56.537Z","request_id":"req_011CgtPYfTVbf8sym8HxYnUk"}
